		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5197&amp;p=37605#p37605"><![CDATA[
I've run through quite a bit of fiddling and have some observations, I'm trying to convey this as concisely and fully as possible.<br><br>I have two CPS programs on my laptop: Old (2023.05.08.01) and new (2024.12.20.01).<br><br>I originally loaded firmware onto my MD-9600 back when the old CPS was current, sorry, don't have the old firmware version. Current firmware on the MD-9600 is 20240323161355 [ 115b17b D ] HW v5 CPU:TYT.<br><br>There was a glitch in the old CPS that permitted one to tab into the fields of the channel setup screen and enter non-standard DCS codes. The MD-9600 pretty much worked with this arrangement and allowed me to work repeaters using non-standard DCS codes. Now and then it would forget to open squelch for any (not just non-standard "wildcat") DCS codes and it would have to have the codeplug refreshed to restore operation. CTCSS codes would work, but any DCS codes would fail to open squelch when it malfunctioned. When I updated to the new CPS I lost the ability to tab into the channel and enter wildcat DCS codes, but the newest CPS and firmware calmed the glitches for the most part and improved functionality. Through run of the mill corruption I lost the functionality for a time, before I remembered that I had a backup of the old CPS stored elsewhere. The interim solution worked well; I use the old CPS to restore the wildcat DCS codes and make any other changes/additions, then store the file, and use the new CPS to upload the revised codeplug to the radio. The MD-9600 stores, Tx, and Rx wildcat DCS codes with no issues now. For the most part the MD-9600 performs to the full possibility of the OpenGD77 setup and I love it.<br><br>Then I bought a Baofeng DM-1701 and uploaded the newest firmware (20241215112702 [2dc33f6 D] CPU:TYT) and have found that with the same codeplug everything works except for the wildcat DCS codes. Is this a hardware limitation? The wildcat codes will upload and store and display on the HT, but transmit and receive do not function. I am considering purchasing a TYT MD-UV390 explicitly to get full functionality from a handheld, because aside from the lack of functionality for this one club's repeaters the software is phenomenal. Given that TYT works and Baofeng doesn't with these two models, it lends itself that the TYT handheld will perform where the Baofeng fell short. Options/opinions?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6008">K3SAD</a> — Mon Jun 30, 2025 3:58 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
